{"type":"text","timestamp":1790854292823,"sessionID":"ses_f08c46ba3ffeXIM05O83TMKJzd","part":{"id":"prt_0f73be0d10016Eba0R5PEN8b2M","messageID":"msg_0f73bb0e0001BzHNNlm2HATu3P","sessionID":"ses_f08c46ba3ffeXIM05O83TMKJzd","type":"text","text":"The bug is clear: `overlaps` uses `<=`, which treats touching intervals (e.g., [0,1) and [1,2)) and empty intervals (e.g., [2,2) vs [1,3)) as overlapping. For half-open intervals sharing an integer point, the condition must be strict: `max(starts) < min(ends)`. I'll make that minimal edit, preserving the API and `span`. {\"action\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"intervals.py\",\"old\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) <= min(left[1], right[1])\",\"new\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) < min(left[1], right[1])\"}","time":{"start":1790854291665,"end":1790854292812}}}
